&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note 1. Organization and Nature of Business&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;PPG Shawville Pipeline LLC (&amp;#8220;PSP&amp;#8221; or the &amp;#8220;Company&amp;#8221;), formerly known as Greylock Shawville Pipeline, LLC (&amp;#8220;GSP&amp;#8221;), formerly known as First ECA Midstream LLC (&amp;#8220;FECAM&amp;#8221;), is a wholly owned subsidiary of Penn Production Group LLC (&amp;#8220;PPG&amp;#8221;).&amp;#160;&amp;#160;Membership units are held by PPG, a Pennsylvania limited liability company.&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;PSP is a natural gas gathering and transmission company subject to the jurisdiction of the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission (&amp;#8220;FERC&amp;#8221;).&amp;#160;&amp;#160;PSP owns and operates an interstate 19-mile pipeline in Clearfield County, Pennsylvania (&amp;#8220;Clearfield System&amp;#8221;).&amp;#160;&amp;#160;The pipeline is used for the transmission of natural gas from producing wells own by certain subsidiaries of PPG for delivery to the interstate pipeline system of BHE GT&amp;amp;S, a Berkshire Hathaway Energy Company.&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;In addition to the transmission and delivery from PPG wells, PSP provides up to 152,000 dekatherms per day of firm transportation service to Shawville Power, LLC (&amp;#8220;Shawville Power&amp;#8221;).&amp;#160;&amp;#160;Shawville Power, formerly known as GenOn REMA, LLC (&amp;#8220;REMA&amp;#8221;), leases and operates a coal-fueled power plant in Shawville, Pennsylvania (&amp;#8220;Shawville Plant&amp;#8221;).&amp;#160;&amp;#160;REMA added natural gas fuel capability to the Shawville Plant, which is provided by PSP&amp;#8217;s natural gas pipeline in Clearfield County, Pennsylvania.&amp;#160;&amp;#160;The Clearfield System began service as a jurisdictional interstate pipeline on September 26, 2016, when the 3-mile section of the pipeline owned by NRG ECA Pipeline LLC and leased to REMA (the &amp;#8220;Lateral-Lane&amp;#8221;) between the existing Clearfield System and REMA&amp;#8217;s Shawville Plant was fully constructed and placed in service.&amp;#160;&amp;#160;PSP charges Shawville Power an annual capacity lease charge in addition to a negotiated per/Dth transportation charge.&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;Effective December 31, 2018, Greylock Midstream acquired the outstanding interest in NRG ECA Pipeline LLC, owner of the Lateral-Line.&amp;#160;&amp;#160;Effective March 31, 2019, NRG ECA Pipeline LLC was merged into GSP, resulting in the combination of the Clearfield System and Lateral-Line in a single 19-mile transmission pipeline covered by GSP&amp;#8217;s certificate and tariff issued by the FERC (the &amp;#8220;GSP&amp;#8221; Transmission Line&amp;#8221;).&amp;#160;&amp;#160;As a result of this combination, the annual capacity release charge and negotiated per/Dth transportation charge charged to Shawville Power were revised to account for the entire GSP Transmission Line.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;Effective August 3, 2021, two new officers were appointed by the Board of Managers per the language of the new and amended operating agreement.&amp;#160;&amp;#160;Josh L. Hull was appointed as the Chief Executive Officer and Eric A. Kowalski was appointed as the Chief Financial Officer and Secretary.&amp;#160;&amp;#160;See Note 7 for more information with regards to the acquisition.&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;Effective September 1, 2021, the name of the Company was changed to PPG Shawville Pipeline LLC.&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note 2.&amp;#160;&amp;#160;Summary of Significant Accounting Policies&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;&lt;em&gt;Basis of Presentation&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;Accounting records are maintained in accordance with the FERC Uniform System of Accounts which is a comprehensive basis of accounting other than accounting principles generally accepted in the United States of America ("US GAAP").&amp;#160;&amp;#160;A significant difference between the Uniform System of Accounts and US GAAP is the presentation of credit balances in asset accounts and debit balances in liability accounts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;GAAP requires that certain account balances within financial statement line items which are not in the natural position for that line item (i.e., an account within Accounts Receivable with a credit balance) be reclassed to the appropriate side of the Balance Sheet.&amp;#160;&amp;#160;FERC does not require certain accounts which are not in a natural position for their respective line item to be reclassed, as long as, the line item in total is in its natural position.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;&lt;em&gt;Use of Estimates&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;The preparation of financial statements in conformity with the FERC Uniform System of Accounts requires management to make estimates and assumptions that affect the reported amounts of assets and liabilities at the date of the financial statements and the reported amounts of revenues and expenses during the reporting year.&amp;#160;&amp;#160;Actual results could differ from those estimates.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;&lt;em&gt;Operating Revenue&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;Operating revenues are recognized as income when the recognition criteria of ASC 606 are met, which generally occurs at the point in which the gas is gathered and transported.&amp;#160;&amp;#160;Operating revenues on gathering and transportation services provided to Penn Production and Shawville Power are based on agreed-upon firm transportation rates.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;&lt;em&gt;Customer Concentration&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;Penn Production and Shawville Power accounted for 100% of the revenues during the year.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;&lt;em&gt;Income Taxes&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;As a limited liability company, PSP is a disregarded entity for federal income tax purposes.&amp;#160;&amp;#160;All items of taxable income and expense pass through to the members of PSP; therefore, income taxes are not reflected in PSP's separate financial statements prepared in accordance with GAAP.&amp;#160;&amp;#160;For FERC purposes, PSP accounts for income taxes based on an asset and liability approach.&amp;#160;&amp;#160;Under this approach, deferred tax assets and liabilities are recognized based on future tax consequences attributable to differences between financial statement carrying amounts of assets and liabilities and their respective tax basis.&amp;#160;&amp;#160;Deferred tax assets and liabilities are measured using PSP's statutory tax rate.&amp;#160;&amp;#160;For the periods ended December 31 2025, PSP had deferred tax liabilities of $25,223,798 and as of December 31, 2024, PSP had deferred tax liabilities of $26,160,568.&amp;#160;&amp;#160;These deferred tax liabilities are the result of depreciation-related timing differences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;All current receivables and payables are shown as such in the current year and it will be settled through equity in the following year.&amp;#160;&amp;#160;The Company has recorded taxes payable in taxes accrued of the accompanying balance sheet.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;&lt;em&gt;Provision for Income Taxes&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;&lt;em&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;table class="MsoNormalTable" style="caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid; width: 448pt; border-collapse: collapse;" border="0" width="597" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0"&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr style="height: 16pt;"&gt;
&lt;td style="width: 217pt; border: 1pt solid white; background: white; padding: 0in 5.4pt; height: 16pt;" nowrap="nowrap" width="289"&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: 12pt; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;"&gt;&lt;span style="color: black;"&gt;For the quarters ended&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
