&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;&lt;em&gt;Impairment of Long-Lived Assets&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;The Company evaluates its long-lived assets for impairment when events or changes in circumstances indicate that the carrying value of such assets may not be recoverable.&amp;#160;&amp;#160;The determination of whether impairment has occurred is based on the Company&amp;#8217;s estimate of undiscounted future cash flows attributable to the assets as compared to the carrying value of the assets.&amp;#160;&amp;#160;The amount of impairment recognized would be the excess of the carrying amount of the assets over the fair value of the assets, as determined either through reference to similar asset sales or by estimating the fair value using a discounted cash flow approach.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;For the period ended December 31, 2025, the Company recognized no impairment losses on long-lived assets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;&lt;em&gt;Long-Term Debt&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;PPG Shawville Pipeline LLC and its parent, Penn Production Group LLC, are joint holders of a long-term debt convertible note facility used to fund the purchase the assets from Greylock Pipeline.&amp;#160;&amp;#160;Effective April 20, 2022, the lender of the convertible note facility converted $900,000 of principal debt into equity membership interests of the parent company, Penn Production Group, LLC.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;&lt;em&gt;Environmental Matters&amp;#160;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;The Company is continually taking actions it believes necessary in its operations to ensure conformity with applicable federal, state and local environmental regulations.&amp;#160;&amp;#160;As of December 31, 2025, the Company had not been fined or cited for any environmental violations, which would have a material adverse effect upon capital expenditures, operating results, or the competitive position of the Company.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;&lt;em&gt;Asset Retirement Obligations&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;Companies are required to record the fair value of a liability related to the retirement of long-lived assets at the time a legal obligation is incurred, if the liability can be reasonably estimated.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;The Company&amp;#8217;s operating assets generally consist of underground natural gas pipelines and related facilities along rights-of-way.&amp;#160;&amp;#160;The Company&amp;#8217;s right-of-way agreements do not require the dismantling, removal and reclamation of the right-of-way upon permanent removal of the pipelines and related facilities from service.&amp;#160;&amp;#160;Additionally, PSP is unable to predict when, or if, the pipelines and related facilities would become completely obsolete and require decommissioning.&amp;#160;&amp;#160;Accordingly, the Company has not recorded a liability or corresponding asset as an asset retirement obligation as both amounts and timing of such potential future costs are indeterminable.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note 3. Revenue from Contracts with Customers&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;The Company&amp;#8217;s revenue is generated from contracts to provide firm gathering and transportation services on pipelines owned by the Company.&amp;#160;&amp;#160;These contracts guarantee access to the pipeline, which can be guaranteed by a fixed reservation fee, and obligate the customer to pay volumetric-based fees, which are charges for the volume of gas gathered or transported. The contracts specify a delivery point which represents the point at which control of the product is transferred to the customer. The performance obligation for the delivery of natural gas is satisfied at a point in time when the natural gas is delivered to the designated sales point.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;The performance obligation for volumetric-based fee revenue is generally satisfied upon the Company's monthly billing to the customer for volumes gathered or transported during the month.&amp;#160;&amp;#160;Revenue related to gathering and transportation services provided but not yet billed is estimated each month.&amp;#160;&amp;#160;The amount billed corresponds directly to the value of the Company's performance to date as the customer obtains value as each volume is gathered or transported.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;Revenue is measured based on the consideration specified in the contract with the customer.&amp;#160;&amp;#160;The Company recognized revenue in the amount that reflects the consideration in expects to receive for the transferring the product to the customer.&amp;#160;&amp;#160;Payment is typically received 10 to 15 days after the end of the calendar month in which the natural gas is delivered.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;Receivables from contracts with customers are recorded when the right to consideration becomes unconditional, generally when control of the product has been transferred to the customer or transported on various pipelines in which the Company charges a fee but does not take title to the gas.&amp;#160;&amp;#160;Receivables from contracts with customers were, $16,929 and $42,509 as of December 31, 2025, and December 31, 2024, respectively, and are reported in accounts receivable on the accompanying balance sheets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note 4.&amp;#160;&amp;#160;Risk Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;&lt;em&gt;Concentration of Credit Risk&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;Cash of the FERC-certified pipeline is funded by the Company and distributed to its parent, Penn Production Group.&amp;#160;&amp;#160;The Company maintains its cash accounts primarily with a single bank, which the Company believes to have minimal risk.&amp;#160;&amp;#160;The Company currently gathers and transports gas production for Penn Production Group and Shawville Power.&amp;#160;&amp;#160;The risk of nonpayment is minimal and is considered when evaluating the adequacy of the Company&amp;#8217;s allowance for doubtful accounts.&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note 5.&amp;#160;&amp;#160;Related Party Transactions&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;PSP gathers and transports natural gas from producing well owns by subsidiaries of Penn Production Group for an agreed-upon gathering rate.&amp;#160;&amp;#160;The amounts owed to PSP by the subsidiaries of Penn Production Group as of December 31, 2025, was $21,819.&amp;#160;&amp;#160;The amounts owned to PSP by PPG subsidiaries of December 31, 2024, was $14,078, which are included in accounts receivable on the accompanying balance sheets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note 6.&amp;#160;&amp;#160;Commitments and Contingencies&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;Effective December 17, 2015, Energy Corporation of America, NRG ECA Pipeline LLC and GenOn Energy, Inc. entered into an agreement with the Company. Under this agreement, the Company agreed to modify its existing Clearfield Pipeline System to provide firm capacity to GenOn's subsidiary REMA. The agreement commenced on September 26, 2016, when the pipeline between the Clearfield Pipeline System and REMA's Shawville Power Plant was fully constructed and placed in service.&amp;#160;&amp;#160;The Company filed for FERC certification of the Clearfield Pipeline System on December 18, 2015, and FERC certification was granted on June 1, 2016.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;Effective June 1, 2019, the preexisting firm transportation agreements between the Company, REMA and Greylock Production, LLC, successor to Energy Corporation of America, were amended and restated to cover the entirety of the Greylock Pipeline Transmission Line.&amp;#160;&amp;#160;On July 30, 2019, REMA transferred the agreement to Shawville Power.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;Effective August 3, 2021, the preexisting firm transportation agreements between the Company, Shawville Power and Penn Production Group were transferred.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note 7.&amp;#160;&amp;#160;Rate and Other Regulatory Matters&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;On December 18, 2015, under Docket No. CP16-35-000, FECAM filed an application pursuant to section 7(c) of the Natural Gas Act and Part 157 of the Commission's regulations, for a certificate of public convenience and necessity authorizing FECAM to operate an existing 16-mile, 4-to16-inch-diameter pipeline in Clearfield and Elk Counties, Pennsylvania ("Existing Pipeline"), as an interstate pipeline. Prior to FERC certification, the Existing Pipeline was solely used for the gathering of natural gas from producing wells owned by FECAM's affiliate, ECA, for delivery to the interstate pipeline systems of Dominion Transmission, Inc. ("Dominion") and National Fuel Gas Supply Corporation ("National Fuel"). FECAM proposed to operate its Existing Pipeline as a jurisdictional interstate pipeline so that it could also receive natural gas from Dominion for delivery to a power plant operated by NRG REMA LLC in Shawville, Pennsylvania. On June 1, 2016, FERC granted FECAM's request to convert its Existing Pipeline to interstate service.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;On November 21, 2016, under Docket No. AC17-29-000, FECAM requested a waiver to file FERC Form 3-Q for third quarter 2016. FECAM began service as a jurisdictional interstate pipeline on September 26, 2016, and proposed including data from its service provided from September 26-30, 2016, on its fourth quarter Form 3-Q/Form 2-A.&amp;#160;&amp;#160;On December 22, 2016, FERC granted the waiver. As such, FECAM included data from September 26-30, 2016, on its fourth quarter Form 3-Q/Form 2-A.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;On April 14, 2017, under Docket No. AC17-99-000, FECAM requested an extension of time to file the 2016 FERC Form 2-A due to difficulties with the submission software.&amp;#160;&amp;#160;On April 18, 2017, FERC granted the extension of time until May 2, 2017. FECAM filed its 2016 FERC Form 2-A on May 2, 2017.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;On November 30, 2018, under Docket No. CP19-22-000, Greylock Pipeline and its subsidiary GSP pursuant to Sections 7(b) and 7(c) of the Natural Gas Act and Parts 157 and 284 of the Commission&amp;#8217;s regulations submitted their joint abbreviated application for the authorizations necessary for Greylock Pipeline to transfer to GSP and for GSP to acquire, own, and operate interstate pipeline facilities for the transportation of natural gas in interstate commerce. Greylock Pipeline and GSP have respectfully requested that the Commission issue an order granting the application on or before March 1, 2019.&amp;#160;&amp;#160;The Commission granted the abandonment and transfer of facilities to GSP on April 18, 2019, to be effective March 1, 2019, as requested.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;On December 21, 2018, under Docket No. CP19-33-000, Greylock Pipeline pursuant to Section 7(c) of the Natural Gas Act and Sections 157.205 and 157.208(b) of the Commission&amp;#8217;s regulations submitted their filing for a Prior Notice request for authorization to acquire natural gas pipeline facilities in Clearfield County, Pennsylvania under its blanket certificate obtained in Docket No. CP16-35-000.&amp;#160;&amp;#160;Specifically, Greylock Pipeline proposed to acquire an approximately 3-mile, 16-inch pipeline (&amp;#8220;Lateral Pipeline&amp;#8221;) owned by its affiliate NRG ECA Pipeline LLC, which is connected to its existing interstate pipeline in Clearfield County, Pennsylvania.&amp;#160;&amp;#160;Greylock Pipeline respectfully requested that the Commission issue a notice of its request on or before December 28, 2018, so the 60-day prior notice expired on February 25, 2019, no protests were filed, and the proposed acquisition closed on March 1, 2019.&amp;#160;&amp;#160;The Commission issued a notice of request on December 27, 2018.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;On December 31, 2018, under Docket No. RP19-528-000, Greylock Pipeline pursuant to Rule 207 (a)(5) and Rule 602 of the Commission&amp;#8217;s Rules of Practice and Procedure petitioned the Commission for approval of its Settlement to adjust its recourse rates.&amp;#160;&amp;#160;The Settlement adjusts Greylock Pipeline&amp;#8217;s recourse transportation rates to account for the requirements of the Tax Cuts and Jobs Act and Order No. 849 as well as to reflect the proposed acquisition of the Lateral Pipeline.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;Greylock Pipeline submitted the Settlement in lieu of a general rate change filing under Section 4 of the Natural Gas Act and the one-time report, Form 501-G, pursuant to Order 849. Greylock Pipeline is authorized to represent that its only shippers, REMA and Greylock Production, LLC (&amp;#8220;Greylock Production&amp;#8221;) either support or do not oppose the proposed Settlement.&amp;#160;&amp;#160;The Settlement does not affect Greylock Pipeline&amp;#8217;s negotiated transportation rates with REMA or Greylock Production.&amp;#160;&amp;#160;Greylock Pipeline respectfully requested that the Commission approve the Settlement no later than February 28, 2019, to allow the Settlement to become effective March 1, 2019.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;On March 5, 2019, under Docket No. RP19-528-000, the Commission approved Greylock Pipeline&amp;#8217;s Settlement to adjust its recourse rates, effective as of March 1, 2019.&amp;#160;&amp;#160;Greylock Pipeline was also authorized by the Commission to acquire and add the Lateral Pipeline to its jurisdictional facilities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;On May 17, 2019, under Docket No. RP19-1226-000, Greylock Pipeline submitted new tariff records to reflect revised negotiated rate agreements with REMA and Greylock Production.&amp;#160;&amp;#160;The revisions in the tariff reflect a change in REMA&amp;#8217;s negotiated rate agreement to modify the rates and the identification of its primary delivery point to reflect Greylock Pipeline&amp;#8217;s acquisition of the Lateral Pipeline.&amp;#160;&amp;#160;In addition, the revisions in the tariff reflect a change in Greylock Production&amp;#8217;s negotiated rate agreement to (i) remove the delivery point to Natural Fuel Gas Supply Corporation and (ii) reduce Greylock Production&amp;#8217;s contracted capacity.&amp;#160;&amp;#160;Both negotiated rate agreements had an effective date of March 1, 2019. On July 11, 2019, under the same Docket, Greylock Pipeline filed to revise the proposed March 1, 2019, effective date to June 1, 2019.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;On September 20, 2019, under Docket No. CP16-35-000, Greylock Pipeline submitted its Three-Year Cost and Revenue Compliance Filing as required by Ordering Paragraph (G) of the FERC Order issued on June 1, 2016, in Docket No. CP16-35-000. The filing was approved by the FERC on October 17, 2019.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;On July 24, 2020, under Docket No. RP20-1039-000, Greylock Pipeline filed revised tariff records to reflect a company name change from Greylock Pipeline to GSP. The Commission approved the abandonment by transfer to GSP on April 18, 2019.&amp;#160;&amp;#160;No other substantive changes were made to Greylock Pipeline&amp;#8217;s currently effective tariffs and GSP is not proposing to change its rates. The Commission accepted the tariff records on August 14, 2020, effective August 1, 2020, as requested.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;On February 8, 2021, Greylock Pipeline and several other subsidiaries of Greylock entered into a Purchase Sales Agreement (&amp;#8220;PSA&amp;#8221;) with Penn Production Group LLC to sell certain assets in Clearfield County, Pennsylvania.&amp;#160;&amp;#160;As part of the PSA, Greylock Pipeline agreed to sell its membership interest in Greylock Shawville Pipeline, LLC.&amp;#160;&amp;#160;The sale closed on August 3, 2021, and the name was changed to PPG Shawville Pipeline LLC.&amp;#160;&amp;#160;Tariffs and forms related to the name change and change in ownership were filed with FERC on August 19, 2021, under Docket No. RP21-1040-000.&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;On November 12, 2021, under Docket No. RP22-301-000, filed a compliance filing: NAESB 3.2 standards.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;On December 30,&lt;sup&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/sup&gt;2021, under Docket No. ACC22-29-000, the Company filed an extension of time to file Form 3-Q due to difficulties to access the electronic or editable Form 3-Q in order to input in order to file the quarterly data.&amp;#160;&amp;#160;On January 3, 2021, FERC granted the extension of time until January 31, 2021.&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;On April 11, 2022, through April 14, 2022, a new tap was installed approximately 8 miles south of the EGTS (Medix Run Meter) interconnect.&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;On May 8, 2023, under the current Docket No. CP23-475-000, and pursuant to Section 7(b) of the Natural Gas Act and 18 C.F.R. &amp;#167; 157.18, the Company filed its Abbreviated Application for Abandonment to Transfer Gathering Facilities and Service.&amp;#160;&amp;#160;Subsequently, on June 7, 2023, the Company filed a response to the Commission Staff&amp;#8217;s June 5, 2023, data requests.&amp;#160;&amp;#160;On November 21, 2023, The Company filed a response to the Commission Staff&amp;#8217;s informal data request on the same day.&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;On March 18, 2024, under Docket No. RP24-527-000, and pursuant to Section 4(d) of the Natural Gas Act and 18 C.F.R. &amp;#167; 157.18, the Company filed a Normal Filing to revise the Company&amp;#8217;s tariff records and to update administrative errors.&amp;#160;&amp;#160;One April 4, 2024, the Company received a letter from the Commission to accept the Company&amp;#8217;s 03/18/2024 filing of revised tariff records to update and correct administrative errors under RP24-527.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;On May 8, 2024, under Docket No. RP24-527-000, and pursuant to Section 4(d) of the Natural Gas Act and 18 C.F.R. &amp;#167; 157.18,&amp;#160;the abandonment authority requested by PPG Shawville Pipeline LLC was permitted by the public convenience or necessity, and subject to the conditions of the order.&amp;#160;&amp;#160;This action was taken under 18 C.F.R. &amp;#167; 375.308.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note 8.&amp;#160;&amp;#160;Subsequent Events&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in; font-size: medium; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke- text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid;"&gt;The Company has evaluated subsequent events for disclosures and events through May 27, 2026, and there was no material, subsequent events that required recognition or additional disclosure in these financial statements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
